  LXTUL FAN ON: fan_k=4 mix='all' repel_mode='epivol' repel_lambda=0.1 repel_passes=2 prefix_k=4 ALL eps=0.05 wta_lambda=0.0 (no mixture, no gate: every stream is written into ITS prefix cell through W_prefix[i], the register's 1:1 route, and the coda reads all K; wta_lambda 0: NO responsibility term and NO extra coda pass) LATENT-SELECTED LOOP 'joint': after every pass the M cells of a continuing slot are reset to the winner (train: follow the ROUTER; the teacher is the argmin ||g(cell) - z||^2 on the EMA-prelude target, EMA m=0.996; eval and slots without a target: the router, rank 64, CE onto the teacher at weight 1.0); ONE latent loss at the exit (relaxed WTA eps=0.05, weight 1.0, head reads DETACHED cells: ranks only, no pull on the loop; online floor 0.2 @ 0.1); the coda reads the final winner alone (the coda's CE reaches the loop through the winner) - read fan/lsel_r2, fan/lsel_teacher_router_agree (chance 1/K), fan/lsel_switch_rate, fan/lsel_cell_spread, and at val fan/lsel_teacher_pick_gap - K latent STREAMS per span through the ONE shared core. The streams ARE the Thought Register's cells (fan_k aliases slot_cells, so the message above is this arm's loop); what is NEW is the three things the register did not have. (1) a DIVERSITY term ('epivol') charged after passes 1..2 only, because PLR Thm 4.4 makes the collapse exponential in depth (pass 1 fights L^2, pass 6 fights L^12). (2) the exit WRITE: every stream in its own prefix cell, the register's 1:1 route, so the coda's width is prefix_k=4 and the width partner is the ruler at the same prefix_k. (3) the ORACLE: at every val the coda is re-run once per stream and `fan/oracle_ce` is the per-span minimum. READ `fan/oracle_ce` AGAINST `fan/single_ce` FIRST - if the gap is inside a width control's own CE gain, the streams are copies and the width branch closes, whatever `fan/mixed_ce` says. Then `fan/stream_cos_t{t}` (1.0 = collapsed; the register read 0.94) and `fan/stream_rank_t{t}` (the register read 1.24 of 4) (lab/experiments/planned/2026-09-19-lxtul-fan4.md)
